MERGE benchmark — licence
=========================

  * Source code (all scripts in 01_dataset_construction/, 02_feature_extraction/,
    04_modeling/, 07_baselines/scripts/ and 08_external_validation/scripts/) — MIT,
    in full below.
  * The models in 05_results/trained_models/ and 08_external_validation/models/ — MIT.
    Their candidate pool excludes every alphagenome_* column.
  * Derived tables and figures (03_datasets/, 05_results/, 05_results_alphagenome_average/
    except the file below, 07_baselines/results/, 08_external_validation/cohort/,
    features/ and results/, 06_figures/) — CC BY 4.0.
    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
  * 05_results_alphagenome_average/alphagenome_reference_quantiles.json — CC BY-NC 4.0.
    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/
    It contains no trained model, but it summarizes AlphaGenome output, whose API is
    offered for non-commercial use.
  * The precomputed scores described in 09_precomputed_scores/ (two .csv.gz files,
    release assets of github.com/XiaoYangGao0401/MERGE-precomputed-scores) — CC BY-NC 4.0. Besides the MERGE scores
    they contain AlphaGenome, dbNSFP (AlphaMissense, ESM-1b) and Nucleotide Transformer
    outputs, whose sources restrict commercial use.
  * Scores of third-party tools extracted for the benchmark variants
    (07_baselines/scores/, 07_baselines/cadd_raw/, 08_external_validation/model_outputs/),
    the columns of 03_datasets/ and 08_external_validation/features/ taken from dbNSFP
    (AlphaMissense_score, ESM1b_score) or the AlphaGenome API (alphagenome_*), and the
    Findlay et al. (2018) supplementary table (08_external_validation/source/) remain
    under the terms of their sources.

None of this relicenses the upstream models, databases or services the pipeline uses.
AlphaGenome, Nucleotide Transformer (v1 and v2), dbNSFP, CADD and ANNOVAR restrict
commercial use. See README.md and
https://github.com/TheFangLab/MERGE/blob/main/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

Not a medical device. Not for clinical use.


